1
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:12,750
You have to do this.

2
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:19,880
I want your team to understand the skill and competition of European football.

3
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,090
Genzo.

4
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:25,470
Mikami-san.

5
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:29,390
I'm sorry I had to make you the bad guy here.

6
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:32,690
It's fine. Did it go the way you wanted?

7
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:37,440
I think I've broken the team apart.

8
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:39,360
It's their first heavy defeat.

9
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:45,700
It depends on whether they realize once again that they lack teamwork.

10
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:49,580
Still, I didn't expect it to turn into a physical fight.

11
00:00:50,910 --> 00:00:53,290
You know, I think Hyuga has matured.

12
00:00:53,370 --> 00:00:54,210
Huh?

13
00:00:54,290 --> 00:00:58,670
I know I called him a coward, but actually I was very happy.

14
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:05,640
The gap between us was huge, but he managed to score a goal for his teammates.

15
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:10,350
He's definitely matured, both mentally and physically.

16
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:13,810
You know, today's injuries and your fight reminded me of when you first came to Hamburg.

17
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,480
What? Ah, those days...

18
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:19,480
They didn't want me to train with Schneider.

19
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:27,120
Hans and the others decided to beat me up.

20
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:29,870
And I had to retaliate.

21
00:01:34,210 --> 00:01:36,420
Whenever you want a fight, I'm ready!

22
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:40,380
Genzo.

23
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:44,050
Whenever you want a fight, I'm ready!

24
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:48,140
By the way, Mikami-san.

25
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:54,020
What do you think about me playing for the Japan team?

26
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:05,270
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

27
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:28,470
Episode 4: A Fresh Start from Zero

28
00:03:30,690 --> 00:03:32,480
They destroyed us.

29
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:36,440
We probably can't compete with European football.

30
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:39,900
Worst of all, our main goalkeeper Wakashimazu is injured.

31
00:03:39,990 --> 00:03:42,030
What the hell are we going to do now?

32
00:03:43,450 --> 00:03:45,910
We only lost one match. Don't feel so sorry for yourselves!

33
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,200
Matsuyama.

34
00:03:47,290 --> 00:03:50,580
This match showed us how they play.

35
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:53,580
We'll work harder.

36
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:54,710
Right.

37
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:57,590
Matsuyama is right.

38
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:00,420
We just have to try again.

39
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:03,680
Optimistic as always, Tsubasa, aren't you?

40
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:04,720
Huh?

41
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,220
Yeah, right.

42
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,180
Good for you!

43
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:19,320
Captain!

44
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:21,990
How's your wound?

45
00:04:22,070 --> 00:04:23,990
Nothing serious.

46
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:28,280
No damage to the bone, so I could be ready for the matches in France.

47
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:32,080
So be it.

48
00:04:32,370 --> 00:04:37,000
It was 6-1, you scored 1 goal.

49
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:42,970
Yes, but as Wakabayashi said, it was a gift.

50
00:04:44,550 --> 00:04:47,090
Tell the truth, Wakashimazu.

51
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:52,350
My Tiger Shot and Schneider's fire shot...

52
00:04:52,930 --> 00:04:54,350
Which is stronger?

53
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:56,270
Captain...

54
00:04:57,400 --> 00:05:00,360
The fire shot is stronger.

55
00:05:01,150 --> 00:05:04,360
Got it. I wanted to know that.

56
00:05:05,450 --> 00:05:10,120
If someone's shot is stronger, then I can still improve mine.

57
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:15,120
I'll train more until I surpass Schneider.

58
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,170
Captain.

59
00:05:18,630 --> 00:05:21,840
Oh, by the way, this came for you.

60
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:22,880
For me?

61
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:24,130
From Coach Kira.

62
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:27,260
This...

63
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:31,180
The third day.

64
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:38,060
The Japan youth team plays its second match against Bremen youth.

65
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:42,150
I didn't mention it before, but we have two matches today.

66
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:47,280
The Italian youth, who are also in the tournament, are here for a trial match.

67
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:53,450
Today, three teams will play alternately against each other.

68
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:57,750
The Italian team and their goalkeeper.

69
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:04,510
It's gotten very interesting, we're playing two matches today.

70
00:06:04,590 --> 00:06:06,880
We'll show them our style of play!

71
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:08,380
Yeah!

72
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:11,890
I thought they might be demoralized yesterday.

73
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:14,180
But it seems their spirits are very high.

74
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:19,150
Hyuga-kun and Matsuyama-kun look tired from yesterday's match.

75
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:21,860
Actually, not from the match.

76
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:25,860
They trained until late last night.

77
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:27,280
Eh! What did you say?

78
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:33,280
Actually three people, not two. Right, Tsubasa-kun?

79
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:35,240
Misugi-kun.

80
00:06:36,910 --> 00:06:41,630
I was working on a squad for the Japan team at that time when...

81
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:49,010
Who is it at this hour?

82
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:52,220
I am the new captain.

83
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:57,140
I don't have an excess of natural talent.

84
00:06:57,230 --> 00:07:00,350
I must work harder and train more to earn everyone's trust and become a true captain.

85
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:08,400
Kojiro, I wanted to send this earlier, but this is from me for Toho's victory.

86
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:13,700
Don't allow yourself to complain.

87
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:15,740
First Japan, then the world.

88
00:07:15,830 --> 00:07:18,080
I want you to work harder than ever before.

89
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:21,170
So you become the best striker the world has ever seen.

90
00:07:23,170 --> 00:07:26,880
This gift is from Coach Kira.

91
00:07:33,430 --> 00:07:36,010
This ball is three times heavier.

92
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:41,390
I want to start from zero and completely overhaul my training.

93
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:43,690
Then a new shot...

94
00:07:44,730 --> 00:07:47,190
I will perfect my new Tiger Shot.

95
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:52,990
Wow, I can really feel it.

96
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:58,580
But I'll train until this ball feels as light as a feather.

97
00:07:59,290 --> 00:08:00,330
Hyuga.

98
00:08:01,790 --> 00:08:02,920
Matsuyama.

99
00:08:04,210 --> 00:08:07,630
I think we're thinking the same thing.

100
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:11,380
- Victory for Japan. - Victory for Japan.

101
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:17,430
Hyuga-kun, Matsuyama-kun.

102
00:08:18,810 --> 00:08:22,140
Hyuga, Matsuyama, and Tsubasa-kun.

103
00:08:22,230 --> 00:08:27,940
When these three work together, the Japan youth team will be complete.

104
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,280
Alright, we've arrived.

105
00:08:34,570 --> 00:08:37,030
This is Bremen Stadium.

106
00:08:37,370 --> 00:08:40,870
Wow, how cool!

107
00:08:41,870 --> 00:08:43,040
Look at that!

108
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:46,040
How passionate the German fans are.

109
00:08:46,330 --> 00:08:48,840
I wonder if they'll talk to me too.

110
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:49,920
Idiot.

111
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,050
Why would they talk to you?

112
00:08:52,670 --> 00:08:54,010
Wakabayashi.

113
00:08:54,090 --> 00:08:54,970
Hello.

114
00:08:55,050 --> 00:08:56,970
Why is he here?

115
00:08:57,890 --> 00:09:01,640
They're not interested in you, they love him.

116
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:06,230
Schester!

117
00:09:06,310 --> 00:09:12,280
Franz Schester, the star player of the 2nd team Bremen youth.

118
00:09:12,570 --> 00:09:14,700
He is their midfielder and star captain.

119
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:19,160
Along with Kaltz and Schneider, he plays for the German youth team.

120
00:09:20,030 --> 00:09:21,410
He's heading this way.

121
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,210
Welcome to Bremen.

122
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:26,870
I'm coach Dreimüller.

123
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:28,710
Nice to meet you.

124
00:09:28,790 --> 00:09:30,040
Nice to meet you too.

125
00:09:33,130 --> 00:09:34,170
Nice to meet you.

126
00:09:36,090 --> 00:09:38,180
Isn't he the captain?

127
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:39,970
I am the captain.

128
00:09:40,350 --> 00:09:41,470
Oh, I'm sorry.

129
00:09:41,930 --> 00:09:42,970
Nice to meet you.

130
00:09:47,270 --> 00:09:49,730
The Italian team is here.

131
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:53,030
The first match is Japan against Bremen.

132
00:09:53,110 --> 00:09:57,860
10 minutes until the match. You can use the field for training until then.

133
00:09:57,990 --> 00:09:59,240
Understood, and thank you.

134
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,540
What's wrong, Schester?

135
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:08,960
Nothing. I just thought that person was the captain.

136
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:17,340
Tsubasa!

137
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:21,450
We haven't trained together like this for a long time.

138
00:10:21,510 --> 00:10:22,350
Yes.

139
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:29,520
What's wrong, Hyuga?

140
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,520
Nothing.

141
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:35,280
Alright, everyone gather up.

142
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:39,030
I want to announce the squad for our first match.

143
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:45,660
Goalkeeper: Morizaki. Defense: Jito, Soda, Izawa, Ishizaki.

144
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:49,290
Midfield: Matsuyama, Sawada, and Sano.

145
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:53,040
Forwards: Kizugi, Taki, Hyuga.

146
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:54,460
That's all for now.

147
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:57,670
Then Tsubasa...

148
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:02,050
Mikami-san, I have something to say too.

149
00:11:02,510 --> 00:11:06,430
Starting today, I'm playing for the Japan team.

150
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,810
Wakabayashi!

151
00:11:08,060 --> 00:11:10,560
And I intend to play for Japan in the French Youth Tournament as well.

152
00:11:10,650 --> 00:11:13,270
- We're counting on you. - What?

153
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,530
Wakabayashi.

154
00:11:15,610 --> 00:11:16,570
Wakabayashi!

155
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:20,030
Mikami-san, is Tsubasa on the bench again today?

156
00:11:20,490 --> 00:11:24,990
I heard it's because he didn't attend the camp before the tournament.

157
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:28,290
Why are you so hung up on this ridiculous thing?

158
00:11:28,370 --> 00:11:32,330
This team was formed 10 days ago.

159
00:11:32,580 --> 00:11:38,090
It makes no sense not to use a talented Japanese player.

160
00:11:38,630 --> 00:11:40,090
Wakabayashi-kun.

161
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:42,720
Let's leave this discussion for later.

162
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:46,430
For now, there will be no changes to today's list. Understood, guys?

163
00:11:46,510 --> 00:11:47,350
Yes, coach.

164
00:11:52,650 --> 00:11:53,900
Hyuga.

165
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,360
Wakabayashi.

166
00:11:55,730 --> 00:11:58,780
I'll be back as soon as I recover.

167
00:11:59,150 --> 00:12:03,360
I won't give up the number 1 goalkeeper jersey that easily.

168
00:12:04,070 --> 00:12:05,370
Wakashimazu.

169
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:08,950
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

170
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:13,960
Born: February 4, Height: 178 cm, Weight: 72 kg, Blood Type: O

171
00:12:14,770 --> 00:12:18,150
The second match of the European tournament.

172
00:12:18,270 --> 00:12:21,780
It begins between Japan youth and Bremen youth.

173
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:21,780
Japan vs Bremen

174
00:12:22,030 --> 00:12:23,780
Let's see what they can do.

175
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:28,780
Number 10, the kid from yesterday.

176
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:32,910
Alright guys, we're playing in this magnificent stadium.

177
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,290
Let's win today.

178
00:12:34,410 --> 00:12:35,250
Okay!

179
00:12:35,330 --> 00:12:36,920
Leave this to us, Tsubasa.

180
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,880
Matsuyama, as captain, do you have anything to say?

181
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:40,800
Yes.

182
00:12:41,170 --> 00:12:44,720
I think we all know what we're up against here in Europe.

183
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:48,050
Even if we can't score, let's beat them with our spirit.

184
00:12:48,390 --> 00:12:49,640
Alright!

185
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:54,500
Those from the German youth team awaiting Japan...

186
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:54,500
Japan squad

187
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:57,690
Captain Schester and forward Margas.

188
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:57,690
Bremen squad

189
00:12:58,230 --> 00:13:00,310
- Let's go, Margas. - Okay.

190
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:03,730
And with the referee's whistle, it begins.

191
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,820
Bremen kicks off.

192
00:13:06,070 --> 00:13:07,660
Let's crush them.

193
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,070
Alright!

194
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:11,080
The Japan team moves forward.

195
00:13:11,330 --> 00:13:13,080
Catch, here it comes!

196
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,580
Hyuga executes a quick long flip.

197
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:21,790
Schester easily takes his position.

198
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:22,800
What!?

199
00:13:26,630 --> 00:13:27,800
That move!

200
00:13:28,050 --> 00:13:31,550
In the first half, Japan couldn't compete with Schester.

201
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:36,060
He completely dominated the midfield and delivered accurate passes.

202
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:38,350
Sometimes he also dribbled past them on his own.

203
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,560
That's a dribble, not a pass!

204
00:13:40,690 --> 00:13:41,650
Woooo hoooo!

205
00:13:41,730 --> 00:13:44,570
Main forward Margas scores the second goal.

206
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:48,320
Now Schester himself scores a goal.

207
00:13:48,570 --> 00:13:50,030
It's 3-0.

208
00:13:50,110 --> 00:13:52,160
With his flawless play.

209
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:55,870
Franz Schester, known as the computer of Bremen.

210
00:13:55,950 --> 00:13:58,040
Schester is so good.

211
00:13:58,250 --> 00:14:01,710
Franz Schester is playing incredibly.

212
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:08,590
Hyuga is quiet today, he seems almost lethargic.

213
00:14:09,090 --> 00:14:13,140
That Schester. He's going to shoot a lot, Hernandez.

214
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:16,560
- We've only just begun. - Yeah!

215
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:21,600
I've always tried to foster independence in the team.

216
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:25,570
And I've always respected the opinions of my players.

217
00:14:25,650 --> 00:14:28,320
They voted for their captain themselves.

218
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:33,370
I won't let Tsubasa play without their approval.

219
00:14:33,450 --> 00:14:35,830
Hurry up, guys, keep fighting.

220
00:14:35,910 --> 00:14:42,120
Ozora Tsubasa, the football genius. The future of the Japan team depends on him.

221
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:48,050
But what about the feelings of the other players? Should I let him play?

222
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:51,430
The whistle for the first half blows.

223
00:14:51,510 --> 00:14:56,430
The Japan team didn't concede more goals, the score remains 3-0.

224
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:58,600
If I had played, then...

225
00:14:58,930 --> 00:15:01,350
Second half! Just watch us in the second half!

226
00:15:01,690 --> 00:15:04,860
But when the second half began...

227
00:15:05,690 --> 00:15:06,730
What!?

228
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:13,490
To prepare for the next match, Bremen substitutes Schester and Margas to the bench.

229
00:15:13,990 --> 00:15:15,490
Who do they think they are!?

230
00:15:17,370 --> 00:15:18,740
Damn it!

231
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:20,500
Tsubasa.

232
00:15:20,790 --> 00:15:22,080
Let's win, guys!

233
00:15:22,170 --> 00:15:23,960
Don't lose to a team like this.

234
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:26,250
Go and do it.

235
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:31,510
Tsubasa's cheering brought excitement back to the Japan team.

236
00:15:31,590 --> 00:15:34,680
Hyuga made a diving header.

237
00:15:34,930 --> 00:15:38,260
Soda overlapped and fired a sharp shot.

238
00:15:38,350 --> 00:15:39,640
They managed to score two goals.

239
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:40,770
Now we'll equalize.

240
00:15:40,850 --> 00:15:43,020
They fell one goal short.

241
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:49,400
So close! The Japan team got to the goal but was too late.

242
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:51,780
The second defeat for Japan's youth.

243
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:55,620
They held on even without Schester and Margas.

244
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:58,160
That shows the strength of German football.

245
00:15:58,280 --> 00:15:59,540
Wakabayashi-kun.

246
00:16:02,210 --> 00:16:04,080
Where are you going, Hyuga?

247
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,710
I'm going back for our match against Italy.

248
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:14,180
While the Japan team was downcast over their two defeats in Europe...

249
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:18,470
the second match between Bremen and Italy began.

250
00:16:14,630 --> 00:16:17,680
Italy squad

251
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:22,980
This is a match that puts both their honor at stake...

252
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:28,940
and a duel between star players Franz Schester and Gino Hernandez.

253
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:30,070
Margas.

254
00:16:31,610 --> 00:16:32,440
Catch!

255
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:35,820
Oh, that goalkeeper...

256
00:16:36,070 --> 00:16:37,280
Great, Gino.

257
00:16:37,370 --> 00:16:39,870
I won't let Italy's goal be breached.

258
00:16:39,990 --> 00:16:41,580
Gino Hernandez.

259
00:16:41,990 --> 00:16:46,210
People say he's Italy's next-generation goalkeeper.

260
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,710
He's famous in Europe.

261
00:16:49,210 --> 00:16:50,920
Emperor Schneider.

262
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:53,550
The computer of Bremen.

263
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:56,510
Europe's number one goalkeeper.

264
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:59,600
I have to get on the field and play.

265
00:17:00,890 --> 00:17:05,560
With the effect of this ball, my leg didn't move comfortably in the game.

266
00:17:06,230 --> 00:17:10,360
But that's the price to pay for getting stronger.

267
00:17:10,610 --> 00:17:15,360
I must keep this up until I perfect my new Tiger Shot.

268
00:17:17,410 --> 00:17:18,490
We did it.

269
00:17:18,570 --> 00:17:22,030
Italy managed to withstand Bremen's fierce attacks.

270
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:25,620
And they managed to score 1 goal on a counterattack.

271
00:17:25,910 --> 00:17:28,620
They won 1-0. Italy is very good.

272
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:36,170
Gino Hernandez. I'll make up for this defeat in the national youth tournament.

273
00:17:36,670 --> 00:17:38,890
So, we're going to play this Italian team?

274
00:17:38,970 --> 00:17:41,050
We have no chance.

275
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:42,260
Guys.

276
00:17:42,350 --> 00:17:44,020
Guys, get dressed.

277
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:47,020
The Italian team won't play against us.

278
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:48,640
What!?

279
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:54,150
They watched our first match and decided they won't gain anything by playing us.

280
00:17:54,530 --> 00:17:56,990
- What!? - They can't do that!

281
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:02,370
Hah, this is better. At least we won't be humiliated.

282
00:18:02,450 --> 00:18:03,580
Soda.

283
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:06,160
Those damn Italian youth.

284
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:08,290
Come here.

285
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:10,370
Italian youth!

286
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:11,790
- What!? - Tsubasa!

287
00:18:12,130 --> 00:18:14,550
Don't underestimate our Japan team.

288
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:18,050
You think you can stop me? Try it then.

289
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:20,640
Who is that? He's coming towards us.

290
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:23,220
Someone stop him.

291
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:25,310
Okay, I'm going.

292
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:27,310
Tsubasa!

293
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:31,560
What? Conti!

294
00:18:31,650 --> 00:18:33,110
- Quick! - Stop him!

295
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:34,480
What happened?

296
00:18:35,570 --> 00:18:36,730
That player!?

297
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:38,990
He wasn't playing in our match.

298
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:49,250
Did he dribble past the whole team?

299
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:51,540
Come on! Catch!

300
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:54,710
His move was amazing!

301
00:18:54,790 --> 00:18:56,300
You did it, Tsubasa!

302
00:18:57,210 --> 00:18:58,300
Shoot!

303
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,550
Gino Hernandez.

304
00:19:00,970 --> 00:19:04,550
Catch, here it comes! Drive Shot!

305
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:14,310
He did it! That's Tsubasa's Drive Shot!

306
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:21,570
What!? Our number one in Europe, Hernandez, couldn't move an inch.

307
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:23,950
Who knew there was a player like this in Asia!?

308
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:25,580
Who is he?

309
00:19:25,950 --> 00:19:28,700
Did you see that, Italian youth?

310
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:32,290
That's Ozora Tsubasa from the Japan team.

311
00:19:32,370 --> 00:19:35,290
- Hooray, Tsubasa! - You're truly amazing.

312
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:37,300
I'm grateful for that.

313
00:19:37,550 --> 00:19:38,500
Ozora...

314
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:39,670
Tsubasa.

315
00:19:40,010 --> 00:19:41,170
Tsubasa.

316
00:19:41,590 --> 00:19:42,680
He hasn't changed at all.

317
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:45,600
Alright, here I come. Come on!

318
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:49,470
He still plays the same way.

319
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,810
Come on!

320
00:19:53,690 --> 00:19:55,560
The Drive Shot, right?

321
00:19:56,730 --> 00:20:00,110
I guess I wasn't mistaken thinking he was the captain.

322
00:20:01,690 --> 00:20:03,450
Guys, listen.

323
00:20:03,950 --> 00:20:09,330
Coach, you won't let Tsubasa play unless we all agree.

324
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:12,000
Please, guys.

325
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:16,130
I don't care if you bench me, just let Tsubasa play.

326
00:20:16,290 --> 00:20:19,420
I can't stand losing anymore.

327
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:24,880
If Tsubasa plays, there's no doubt it will benefit the whole team.

328
00:20:26,010 --> 00:20:31,720
I said Tsubasa had no right to play because he didn't come to camp.

329
00:20:32,140 --> 00:20:35,560
But after seeing Tsubasa's game just now,

330
00:20:35,650 --> 00:20:40,230
I understood he'll make us stronger, so why not.

331
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:41,820
Then...

332
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:47,700
His play now was inspiring, I take back what I said.

333
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,240
Matsuyama-kun.

334
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:51,620
Now only Hyuga remains.

335
00:20:55,290 --> 00:20:56,330
Hyuga-san.

336
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:59,000
- Captain. - I'm not the captain anymore.

337
00:20:59,630 --> 00:21:02,300
I also agree with Matsuyama.

338
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:03,670
Hyuga.

339
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:06,010
Guys, anyone object?

340
00:21:06,180 --> 00:21:07,010
No.

341
00:21:07,090 --> 00:21:10,010
Th-thank you, guys. Thank you.

342
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:12,270
Coach Mikami.

343
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:17,560
The Hamburg club has officially allowed Wakabayashi to play in the national youth tournament.

344
00:21:17,690 --> 00:21:19,520
Good news, Katagiri-kun.

345
00:21:19,810 --> 00:21:21,520
Good news, Katagiri-kun.

346
00:21:22,110 --> 00:21:27,530
If Tsubasa is accepted to play for Japan, then I guess I am too.

347
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:29,780
Yes.

348
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:30,870
Hyuga.

349
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:35,410
And as you said, only highly talented players can be on the field.

350
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:36,580
Hyuga-kun.

351
00:21:36,660 --> 00:21:37,870
Hyuga.

352
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:38,830
Hyuga-san.

353
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,170
A talent war.

354
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:44,510
Right. The real Japan team lineup will be a war of talent.

355
00:21:44,590 --> 00:21:49,050
There's another important player waiting at the final stop of this tournament in France.

356
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:54,430
He is Taro Misaki, waiting for you with his number 11 jersey.

357
00:21:55,270 --> 00:21:57,440
Mi-Misaki? Our Misaki?

358
00:21:57,730 --> 00:22:00,940
Misaki-kun? Really?

359
00:23:44,710 --> 00:23:51,970
NEXT EPISODE: ONE MORE HEAVY GUN